mantle rm237
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_brenna_greyworth
title the stall in a string
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk carries_a_string_measured_to_a_market_stall
likes spiced_cider roof_birds sharp_knife summer_evenings
dislikes haggling cold_tea
fears borrowing_somebody_elses_counter
hopes a_stall_barely_wide_enough_for_two
topics work +0.5 dreams +0.4 animals +0.2 prices +0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=curt refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures unlikely spaces for a future stall, restless at a slow bargain and content to watch a bird choose a perch.

words
oath! = Cross my cord twice | Chalk strike me level
saying! = Nobody can charge rent on string | Room first and wares after
cord = my stall cord | the knotted string
knuckle = a thumb of spare space | a narrow thumb's width
hook = a bent iron peg | a short hook
bag = a worn tool roll | my wrapped tools
stone = a small wet stone | the honing pebble
hem = the hem of the awning | a folded canvas edge
cup = a hot cider cup | a little crock of cider
spice = a fleck of spice | a red speck on the rim
perch = a ridge of slate | a chimney ledge
purse = a stitched coin flap | my inside pocket
change = a loose bit of change | a thin saved copper
wax = a curl of wax | soft comb wax
mark = my width mark | the centre knot

any
opinion houses against 2 : Whoever takes money for a roof can find time to climb under the bit that leaks.
opinion merchants against 1 : Pay me for the time I spent making it. You can talk the ear off a post for free.
opinion road for 1 : A decent road leaves room for me to carry a bundle without being told to tuck my elbows in.
opinion festivals against 1 : Dance all you like. I object to having the end of somebody's dance land in my cider.
opinion dole for 2 : Soup tastes better served before the questions. Ask them after the bowl comes back.
opinion sump for 2 : Down here a wolf shows you the bad board on the landing. Fancy folk pretend theirs are quite sound.

grown
line greet : Move that elbow a shade. There, we're both in. | Welcome. Don't get the knots underfoot.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Room enough for a first word. | A fresh face. Don't let me measure you by mistake.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Early enough to spread my things. | Day's got an empty edge yet.
line greet.return : Heard you before you stepped across my string. | Welcome, within reason and reach.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Say on while the wax settles. | A word fits between jobs. Go on.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Plenty of room for your sort of interruption. | Good. You know which bit to leave clear.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : There's daylight enough left for talk. | Evening. Leave the string where it lies, please.
line again.open : Second visit. You'll be owing me stall rent. | Back inside my measure again.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Sit here, family get the wide end. | I can let my temper out round you.
line farewell : Go on while there's space for passing. | Take your elbow and your good news with you.
line farewell.return : Straight string and a clear way out. | I'll tuck my things in behind you.
line react.news : Give it me by the useful end. | Skip the decoration. I want the happening.
line react.news.new : That's fresh off the reel. | I couldn't have measured for that one.
line react.news.known : Had the length of that already, thanks. | Nothing new between the knots there.
line react.news.doubt : It sounds wider in the telling than it ever stood. | I'd measure that account against another ear.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Ah. That's sore news to rub against. | Put my temper aside a minute. That's bad.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. Some things deserve the whole counter. | That's a bright little copper in a grubby day.
line ask.how : Has anybody left you room to breathe today? | How tight's the day tied you?
line answer.how : Still scratching out a corner for myself. | I've done enough today to soften one knot.
line decline : No, I'd lose my afternoon to that bargain. | Leave me out. I need the time more.
line accept_decline : Saves a stretch of useless bargaining. | Clear answer. I respect that.
line thank : You've freed up a whole paw for me. | I'll count that with the savings.
line deflect_thanks : Fine. Don't spend all afternoon paying for it. | Already done. Leave off reckoning.
line sympathise : Hard to stand straight with so little space left. | Here, put the weight down on my roll.
line preclose : I've got a knot to set before I forget. | I'd best coil this conversation up now.
line accept_preclose : Go settle your business. Mine can wait a minute. | Fine. Take the wide way out.
line ack : Just to the mark. | That width exactly.
scene width
when topic=dreams|work
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This knot's where my future counter ends. | I've nearly got a stall. Only the timber and roof and stock still wanting.
b : Where does it begin? | What's already bought?
a : At the other knot. I can carry the whole place in my pocket. | The length of it. Nobody can argue with the string.

scene two_paws
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've stopped carrying everything in one roll. | Put a stone next to wax and the wax remembers it.
b : Why two rolls? | With a scratch?
a : One takes the things that bend. One takes the things that make them bend. | With a very expensive dent in a very small piece of work.

scene wick_test
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The trouble with a long wick is where to put the end you're not holding. | I twist the thread till both ends want to meet.
b : Could you wear it round your neck? | Then what?
a : Could I? Yes. Will I sell a wick full of red fur? No. | Let them meet. A good cord helps make itself.

scene wax_warm
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #wax.capitalize# wants just the warmth of a closed paw. | I don't want wax either hard or running.
b : What if you overdo it? | A narrow preference.
a : Then I get to scrape my own fingerprints off the work. | A narrow piece of work, as it happens. It deserves one.

scene roof_truce
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd allow a bird one free perch above my future stall. | A bird weighs up a new ledge in a blink.
b : Only one? | Quicker than you?
a : One free at a time. A whole flock would spoil the goods. | Quicker and without string. Irritatingly talented.

scene cider_spice
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I save the last swallow till #spice# has settled. | My cider tastes its loudest right at the bottom.
b : I stir mine. | Loud?
a : Then you get the same ordinary mouthful all the way down. | Hot spice behind the teeth. Hard to hear anything else.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A drawn-out bargain could chill a cup in a furnace. | Wasted my tea talking over a trifle once.
b : Wouldn't it be worth it for a sale? | Did you get the trifle?
a : Only if the buyer paid for the tea as well. | Kept it. It didn't soften the tea any.

scene whetstone
when topic=pastimes self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #stone# in its own wrap. It wears holes in a pocket. | A honing pebble wears down even when the blade looks much the same.
b : Learned that by losing it? | Would you trade for a fresh one?
a : Learned it when a thigh started complaining, actually. | No. This one's learned my grip into both sides.

scene two_coins
when topic=prices
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : The next copper I save buys one imaginary peg for the awning. | I price a dream in little bits. It's less cheeky that way.
b : An imaginary peg is free. | Which bit comes first?
a : Not when it's holding the corner I'm working toward. | The bit I can still afford after supper.

scene bad_offer
when topic=smalltalk|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count to three before answering a silly offer. | A low offer doesn't improve with being repeated louder.
b : What happens on four? | What keeps it steady?
a : I'm usually coiling the string to go elsewhere. | Let the last offer lie there looking embarrassed.

scene dry_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I'd set the awning sloped so the wet runs away from my feet. | Hear the rain strike one patch and skip the next?
b : Onto whose feet then? | A hole?
a : Nobody's, if I measure the gutter first. I'm restless, not heartless. | A high bit. That's the patch I want over my counter.

scene doorsteps
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Sump I've measured market space on a landing for want of better. | Down home my neighbours could tell you my width from all the measuring.
b : Did it fit? | Full width?
a : Half a stall and a very annoyed imaginary customer. | Full dreaming width. Reality might fold in at one side.

scene close_market
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Across the city there's a space that looks ideal until the delivery carts come. | A corner in the Commons is worth visiting at three different hours.
b : Too tight for the wheels? | Why three visits?
a : Just right for wheels. Makes a hopeless stall though. | To see who else thinks it's unoccupied.

scene spring_mark
when topic=season here.season=summer here.time=dusk
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A summer evening leaves time to measure everything again. | Another hour of light and my imagined stall grows a shelf.
b : Doesn't the string stay the same? | A real shelf?
a : The streets don't. They keep filling with other people's ideas. | In my head. A very level one.

scene lean_dream
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Hard times can't take away the width of my string. | I let the market dream run a little short when food's dear.
b : They might wear the string out. | Make a smaller stall?
a : Then I'll remember where its last two knots stood. | Spend less time on it. Supper's a dream with a deadline.

scene private_news
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can keep a secret better than I keep my temper. | I shut my ears when an account gets too personal.
b : What's the trick? | Can you really?
a : A temper gets under my skin. Somebody else's secret belongs under theirs. | Set a little shopping list running inside my skull. Never fails.

scene friendly_loan
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd let #self.friend# sit out a borrowing on my best tool. | I've room in my future plans for a word from #self.friend#.
b : Without a return date? | What sort of word?
a : A loose date. That's quite a stretch for me. | Honest, especially when I've drawn the awning much too grand.

scene visitor
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New here? I'll show you a spot outside a cart's reach. | A new trader shouldn't have to discover every bad corner by falling off one.
b : Which patch is safe? | Wouldn't you want the best corner yourself?
a : The patch the carter can actually see, as a rule. | Yes. But I don't want a rival flattened for my convenience.

scene birds_learn
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I could learn something about haggling from rooftop birds. | Look how a bird vacates a perch without signing anything.
b : Do they offer less seed? | No long argument?
a : They stop paying attention as soon as the bargain looks dull. | One hop. The next one can choose its own direction.
b : You could use that trick yourself. | I'll take a lesson in hopping, then.

story string_shrunk [topic=memories|weather]
  : I washed my first stall cord to make it presentable. Pegged it out to dry, took it off, laid it in its usual place.
  : I'd lost almost a paw's width on the counter and hadn't even got a counter yet.
  b : Did it stretch out again?
  : Not for me. I wound the mean little thing round a parcel and started over.

story empty_hooks [topic=dreams]
  : Once I sat under an empty awning after a sale. All the hooks were bare. I counted what each one might hold.
  : By the time I left I'd stocked an entire stall and quarrelled in my head with two customers.
  b : Did either of them buy?
  : Both. No sense inventing a whole afternoon of losing money.

story bird_coin [topic=memories|animals]
  : A bird once settled beside a copper I had set down. I made a grab, thinking it would fly off with my savings.
  : It was after a crumb under the copper. My grab sent the coin skittering three boards along.
  b : Then who had to look for supper?
  : Me. The bird swallowed the crumb while I was on my knees.

rule @length
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Don't snip before I've laid the cord flat! | One knot free, both ends in plain view.

rule @wrap
when concept=bark self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Soft work gets its own roll. | Keep that corner clear of the wax!

rule @roofbird
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Plenty of ledge for a light caller. | Little perch, large opinion up there.

rule @heat
when concept=bark self.dislikes=cold_tea
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Drink it before the price discussion starts! | Lukewarm bargain, cold supper. Enough.

dlg resident.hub : Step inside my length of string. I've time for whatever's brought you here.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, right on the edge of my calculations.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : After hours is no time to haggle. We can still talk.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it without leaning across my space.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter self.workplace] : #self.workplace#. Wax, cord, the work in front of my paws, then my own dreams after.
dlg resident.job : I make enough space to see what I'm doing.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This has come along: #world.news#. There's the useful length of it.
dlg resident.bye : Lift your foot over the string on the way.
graft resident.hub
choice What are those two knots measuring? -> knot_stall
node knot_stall
say A stall wide enough for my goods and one customer who can make a decision. I've measured the customer generously.
mood keen
free
choice What about a customer who can't decide? -> knot_undecided
choice I'll leave you to your reckoning. -> hub
node knot_undecided
say There's a whole city outside the far knot for thinking things over. Come back under the awning when you've done.
choice I'll bear the far knot in mind. -> hub
choice I know where I stand. -> bye
